WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.089 --> 00:00:08.000
I have another beautiful example, really a
perfect example of these attempts to play

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.500
hardball with Joe Biden's press secretary,
Jen Psaki.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.330
And it is not going well.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:20.070
And this one isn't just Fox News's Peter Doocy
saying something obviously belligerent.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.170
This is a reporter actually trying to make
something that is not controversial, controversial.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:31.070
The question is from Owen Jensen, who is a
reporter for the religious channel EWTN.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:39.710
Own wants to know, how can we be sure that
covid stimulus money in the planned proposed

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.510
one point nine dollars trillion covid relief
bill?

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.450
How can we be sure that none of that money
will go towards abortions?

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.640
Now, Jen Psaki does something smart.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:58.640
She asks, well, what specific sections are
you even referring to where money could go

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.760
to abortion?

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.160
Let's listen and then discuss.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.460
Go ahead, ma'am.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:07.700
Good afternoon on Jensen, EWTN Global Catholic
Network.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:12.450
So regarding the American rescue plan, groups
like pro-life groups, including the Susan

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:18.429
B. Anthony List are very concerned that millions
of U.S. taxpayer dollars will go to the abortion

00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:21.259
industry in violation of the Hyde Amendment.

00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:24.569
We know where President Obama stands on the
Hyde Amendment.

00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:29.069
But that being said, can this administration
right now guarantee if the American rescue

00:01:29.069 --> 00:01:33.329
plan is passed, that no taxpayer dollars will
go to the abortion industry?

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:38.340
Which component of the American rescue plan
are you referring to here?

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:44.819
A 50 million dollar funding increase for the
Title 10 program, 750 million dollars for

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:49.849
global health activities and billions in funding
for community health centers without applying

00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:50.849
the Hyde Amendment.

00:01:50.849 --> 00:01:56.130
Well, the president's view and the Hyde Amendment
is well known, as you have stated in your

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.130
question.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:04.159
He also believes that community health centers
are a key part of addressing the pandemic,

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:10.000
of ensuring that people in communities have
access to vaccines, have access to treatment

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.599
and information about about making sure they
are healthy in their loved ones are healthy.

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:18.140
So that remains a priority to the president.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.620
He's shared his view on the Hyde Amendment.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.230
I don't think I have anything for you.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.879
So, Jen Psaki, later, part of the answer is
sort of OK, but it's her earlier question

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:27.879
that's key.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:32.159
She asks, what parts of covid relief are you
referring to?

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:36.840
And the reporter mentions Title 10 global
health initiatives and funding for community

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.840
health centers.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.620
Now, two of those we can just dismiss out
of hand because there's no evidence.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.750
They don't make sense, he says.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:47.590
Does the money for global health initiatives
maybe go towards abortions?

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.469
There's no reason to think that that's the
case.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:53.700
Does the money for community health centers
maybe go towards abortions absent some reason

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.610
to believe that that funding would go towards
abortion?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.340
I think there's no reason to explore those
any further.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.890
But the interesting one is Title 10.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:05.140
Title 10 is a federal grant program that's
related.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.590
It's related to family planning.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.370
That's true.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:14.959
And it is part of the program that no Title
10 money goes to abortion directly.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:21.200
It is true that because Title 10 provides
money for contraception and family planning,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.690
it reduces pregnancies and thus it reduces
the number of people seeking abortions.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:32.720
And again, some people might say, well, listen,
Title 10 allows money to go to Planned Parenthood

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.060
and Planned Parenthood does abortions.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:43.870
But again, the law is Planned Parenthood can't
use Title 10 money to fund abortions.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:51.909
So this is the same tired talking point, a
talking point about federal funds for abortion

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:57.410
that religious media and Republican politicians
love to trot out whenever the president is

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:01.800
a Democrat, when there actually isn't anything
to discuss.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.620
Title ten money can't go towards abortions.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.590
There's no reason to think that if the title
10 money is in covid relief, it would be any

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.920
different than anything else.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:14.099
Now, one last bonus clip for you from yesterday's
briefing.

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:16.030
Just another silly question.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:22.019
A reporter tries to also play hardball with
Jen Psaki because Joe Biden's planned address

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:26.120
to a joint session of Congress is happening
in March, not in February, as some initially

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:27.210
thought.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.210
And it just.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.210
Kind of goes nowhere.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.210
All right.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.150
Just wanted to follow up on the president's
appearance before a joint session of Congress

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:38.169
and his primetime address last month in January,
reading from prepared remarks, he said, next

00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:42.310
month and my first appearance before a joint
session, I will lay out my build back.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.310
Better plan.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:46.940
So it feels like he did say it was going to
be.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.640
Well, what I was referring to as there was
reporting on February twenty third and I don't

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.330
know where that date came from, which has
never been inaccurate.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.710
So it was the February.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:59.009
Twenty third wasn't just an accurate date,
no one's fault.

00:04:59.009 --> 00:05:00.729
It just it just wasn't it created some confusion.

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:03.550
So I was just trying to clarify it.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.690
Obviously the president looks forward to speaking
to a joint session and we just don't have

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.750
a date yet for when that will be.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:14.660
Jen Psaki continuing to just be kind of like
the mom who's frustrated but trying to remain

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.560
patient with her kids.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.479
Maybe it's just the confusion.

00:05:19.479 --> 00:05:20.860
We're not blaming anybody.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.979
The address by Joe Biden will be in March.

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:25.570
It's not a big deal.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:30.280
And there are rumors, of course, from from
Washington that Joe Biden doesn't want to

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.800
do that address until covid relief is passed.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:37.169
And I would certainly understand that because
the longer it goes without passing covid relief,

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:41.220
the more of the more of an early stain that
that will be on the Biden presidency.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.790
It's time to pass it.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:43.790
It's time to pass it.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.790
I said it yesterday.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.890
I said it the day before.

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.419
I'm not going to keep going on and on.

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:49.520
But it is time to pass covid relief.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:55.250
Remember, during their first year in office,
presidents typically don't do a State of the

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:01.370
Union, but they will sometimes do a joint
address before the House and Senate, not called

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:02.660
a State of the Union.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.040
It could be really at any time.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:12.319
And I am looking forward to seeing Joe Biden's
in March, but really trying to create a controversy

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:14.200
where there isn't one.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:19.759
After the break, we are going to talk about
the latest fabricated scandal from right wing

00:06:19.759 --> 00:06:22.289
media about the Biden administration.

00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:27.620
This one is so stupid that it really shows
you the degree to which the right is desperate

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.289
to create these scandalous narratives.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:07:05.220
We'll take a quick break.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:44.500
We'll be back soon.

